  "result": "I've written the plan to `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\defaults-configured-through-default-map-cozy-swan.md`. The plan-approval tool isn't available in this session, so I'm presenting it here for your go-ahead.\n\n**Cause:** In `Context.__init__` (`src/click/core.py:386-394`), a child context with no `default_map` of its own inherits the parent's whole map. A group's `default_map={\"runserver\": {\"port\": 5000}}` therefore reaches the `runserver` subcommand as the top-level dict. Looking up `port` there finds nothing, so the configured default is ignored.\n\n**Planned fix:**\n1. In `src/click/core.py`, change `default_map = parent.default_map` to `default_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)`. A missing key gives `None`, so no defaults apply, and the existing guards stay.\n2. Add regression tests in `tests/test_defaults.py`:\n   - A subcommand picks up its nested defaults.\n   - A nested group works.\n   - A CLI argument still overrides the default.\n   - A subcommand with no entry is unaffected.\n3. Add a bug-fix entry to `CHANGES.md`.\n4. Verify by running `pytest tests/test_defaults.py tests/test_context.py tests/test_options.py tests/test_commands.py`, then the full suite.\n\nApprove this and I'll implement it.",
